SOCKS grammar reconciliation: expanded the pinned Java 5.5.1 socksConstruction oracle by eight actual constructor inputs, from 78 to 86. The cases cover leading/trailing comments, a comment after a value colon, literal vertical-tab whitespace, unknown string escapes, raw control characters, trailing text, and U+2028 inside strings. The Java fixture records route presence as well as parsed values; client-config fixture SHA-256 is ebdf736dea2b312ca5bf85c678c9eb6fa8713172bd538ca9ee7a00c6836c19d8. Native parsing matches every constructor outcome and reflected route value. The parser rejects Java-disallowed comment placement, vertical-tab whitespace, and unknown escapes, while encoding U+2028 inside strings for the JSON5 backend and preserving its parsed value.

