Endpoint port/scope follow-up (2026-10-08 20:33 UTC): extended the direct Java 5.5.1 endpoint corpus to eleven cases. `NettyRemotingClient.getHostAndPort` splits port zero, 65535, 65536 and -1; the same path reaches `Bootstrap.connect(String,int)`, whose pinned Netty implementation calls `InetSocketAddress.createUnresolved`, so Java accepts 0 and 65535 and rejects values outside the socket-address range. It also directly records Java resolution for raw and bracketed numeric-scoped IPv6 (`%7`). Native parsing now accepts port zero and numeric scope IDs, canonicalizes the scoped address, and rejects out-of-range ports. Named interface scope labels remain unsupported because native name resolution does not preserve their scope reliably. Updated fixture SHA-256: `1de2408296ead009e47827d80f8b279cd779dfa9d50fe375a9ea50a60e5ef187`.

