Fastjson unpaired-surrogate boundary (2026-10-08 20:41 UTC): extended the pinned Java SOCKS constructor corpus from 109 to 111 actual `MQClientInstance` inputs. Java accepts isolated `\uD800` and `\uDC00` escapes, preserves the raw config text, and its reflected `NettyRemotingClient.proxyMap` contains the exact lone UTF-16 code unit. The earlier native differential failed because JSON5/Rust `String` cannot represent these Java values. Native source normalization now replaces only unpaired surrogate escapes in string literals with U+FFFD; valid surrogate pairs remain intact. The native test records this lossy string-value boundary while matching Java's successful construction outcome. Current `client-config.json` SHA-256: `daf340c6136e5081901763a3af9ab93839584a05e5b7873e9752ebd5549ddb29`; [ADR-0036](../../../docs/architecture/ADR-0036-fastjson-surrogate-boundary.md) records the limit.

